 text='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Decowaves individual component review</title><style>body{font:17px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;max-width:1040px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#242c27}article{border-top:1px solid #aaa;margin-top:32px;padding-top:12px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{padding:9px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;overflow-wrap:anywhere}th{width:27%}small{overflow-wrap:anywhere}nav{line-height:2}</style></head><body><h1>Decowaves individual component review</h1><p>Six active finish options across two working design groups, retaining four original component IDs. Each option remains individually offered. Owner confirmed the White/Verdigris number1 and number2 pairs separately. Existing Terracotta memberships are retained without a new photograph approval.</p><nav><a href="decowaves-component-review.csv">Download six-option specifications and links</a> · <a href="index.html">Full terminal walkthrough</a></nav><p>Current master:188 active options and110 working design groups. Decowaves2 Terracotta has no direct option-level offer ref; O060 remains a broader design/arrangement reference, with its Verdigris finish qualified separately.</p>'+''.join(cards)+'<h1>Recorded platform source scope</h1>'+''.join(source_cards)+'</body></html>';page=H/'decowaves-component-review.html';page.write_text(text)
